From: renaud <rlpirou@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:10:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BTC-CORE hooks: player cell change

No option. dev.btc.core.api.event.PlayerCellChangeEvent is fired when a
move takes a player into another block. With no listener registered each
hunk is one static call that reads the length of the listener array and
returns: nothing is computed, allocated or kept on the player.

- ServerGamePacketListenerImpl#handleMovePlayer and #handleMoveVehicle:
  after a PlayerMoveEvent that was neither cancelled nor redirected,
  dev.btc.core.world.CellChanges#moved is given its two locations and
  fires the event when their blocks differ - on the thread that fires
  PlayerMoveEvent.

BTC addition; nothing is ported.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java b/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
index 5e9b3600482923bd54548366b20b797452853a24..9536c4a3c858f54d2f73b76c465af37508f9c9ce 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/network/ServerGamePacketListenerImpl.java
@@ -730,6 +730,7 @@ public class ServerGamePacketListenerImpl
                         this.justTeleported = false;
                         return;
                     }
+                    dev.btc.core.world.CellChanges.moved(player, from, to); // BTCCore - PlayerCellChangeEvent: the move that PlayerMoveEvent let through took the player into another block; nothing computed while no listener is registered
                 }
                 // CraftBukkit end
                 this.player.level().getChunkSource().move(this.player);
@@ -1769,6 +1770,7 @@ public class ServerGamePacketListenerImpl
                             this.justTeleported = false;
                             return;
                         }
+                        dev.btc.core.world.CellChanges.moved(player, from, to); // BTCCore - PlayerCellChangeEvent: the move that PlayerMoveEvent let through took the player into another block; nothing computed while no listener is registered
                     }
                     // Paper end
                     this.player.absSnapTo(targetX, targetY, targetZ, targetYRot, targetXRot);
